{"title":"Career Roadmap · Sports Nutritionist","role":"Sports Nutritionist","summary":"A Sports Nutritionist applies nutrition science to support athletes and physically active individuals with performance, recovery, body composition, hydration, energy availability and long-term health.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc. (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Nutrition & Dietetics"},"about":[{"label":"Important","text":"The exact professional title, registration requirements and scope of practice vary by country and employer. A B.Sc. provides the academic foundation; clinical nutrition roles may require additional qualifications and supervised practice."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Horizons: 2026–2046","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build nutrition, physiology and sports-science foundations"}],[{"text":"2030–2032"},{"text":"Internship + supervised athlete exposure"}],[{"text":"2032–2035"},{"text":"Sports nutrition practice and athlete support"}],[{"text":"2035–2038"},{"text":"Senior sports nutrition / performance nutrition"}],[{"text":"2038–2042"},{"text":"Team-level specialist or private consultancy"}],[{"text":"2042–2046"},{"text":"Performance nutrition leadership, research or entrepreneurship"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build this","Key skills","Proof"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Nutrition fundamentals"},{"text":"Biochemistry, physiology, food science"},{"text":"Nutrition analysis project"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Human nutrition"},{"text":"Macronutrients, micronutrients, assessment"},{"text":"Diet-planning portfolio"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Sports nutrition"},{"text":"Exercise physiology, hydration, recovery"},{"text":"Athlete nutrition case study"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Professional practice"},{"text":"Internship, athlete monitoring, counselling"},{"text":"Sports nutrition internship + capstone"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Nutrition & Human Biology"},{"type":"p","text":"Build a strong scientific foundation."},{"type":"h","text":"Core subjects"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human anatomy"},{"text":"Human physiology"},{"text":"Biochemistry"},{"text":"Food science"},{"text":"Fundamentals of nutrition"},{"text":"Microbiology"},{"text":"Basic chemistry"},{"text":"Psychology"},{"text":"Statistics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Understand the body"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Digestive system"},{"text":"Endocrine system"},{"text":"Musculoskeletal system"},{"text":"Cardiovascular system"},{"text":"Respiratory system"},{"text":"Energy metabolism"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand how the body obtains and uses:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Carbohydrates","glucose","ATP"]},{"type":"flow","items":["Fat","fatty acids","energy"]},{"type":"flow","items":["Protein","amino acids","tissue repair and synthesis"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Human Nutrition"},{"type":"p","text":"Master the fundamentals of nutrition."},{"type":"h","text":"Macronutrients"},{"type":"h","text":"Carbohydrates"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Glycogen"},{"text":"Glucose metabolism"},{"text":"Glycogen storage"},{"text":"Carbohydrate loading"},{"text":"Pre-exercise carbohydrate"},{"text":"During-exercise fueling"},{"text":"Post-exercise recovery"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Protein"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Essential amino acids"},{"text":"Protein quality"},{"text":"Muscle protein synthesis"},{"text":"Protein distribution"},{"text":"Recovery nutrition"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Fats"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Essential fatty acids"},{"text":"Fat oxidation"},{"text":"Dietary fat"},{"text":"Energy density"},{"text":"Role of fats in endurance exercise"}]}]},{"heading":"Micronutrients","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop knowledge of:"},{"type":"h","text":"Vitamins"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Vitamin A"},{"text":"B-complex"},{"text":"Vitamin C"},{"text":"Vitamin D"},{"text":"Vitamin E"},{"text":"Vitamin K"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Minerals"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Iron"},{"text":"Calcium"},{"text":"Magnesium"},{"text":"Zinc"},{"text":"Sodium"},{"text":"Potassium"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Pay particular attention to nutrients relevant to athletic performance and health, such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Iron"},{"text":"Vitamin D"},{"text":"Calcium"},{"text":"Magnesium"},{"text":"Sodium"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Avoid treating supplements as a substitute for identifying an actual dietary deficiency."}]},{"heading":"Year 3 — Sports Nutrition","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Now move from general nutrition to performance nutrition."},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the nutritional requirements of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Strength athletes"},{"text":"Endurance athletes"},{"text":"Team-sport athletes"},{"text":"Combat-sport athletes"},{"text":"Swimmers"},{"text":"Runners"},{"text":"Cyclists"},{"text":"Football/cricket players"},{"text":"Adolescent athletes"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Different sports require different strategies."}]},{"heading":"Exercise Physiology","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ATP-PC system"},{"text":"Anaerobic glycolysis"},{"text":"Aerobic metabolism"},{"text":"VO₂ max"},{"text":"Lactate threshold"},{"text":"Muscle glycogen"},{"text":"Exercise-induced fatigue"},{"text":"Training adaptation"},{"text":"Recovery"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the relationship:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Training","Fuel","Performance","Recovery","Adaptation"]}]},{"heading":"Energy Requirements","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn how to estimate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Basal metabolic rate"},{"text":"Total daily energy expenditure"},{"text":"Exercise energy expenditure"},{"text":"Energy availability"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand why insufficient energy intake can negatively affect:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Performance"},{"text":"Recovery"},{"text":"Hormonal function"},{"text":"Bone health"},{"text":"Immune function"},{"text":"Training adaptation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This is particularly important for athletes undergoing heavy training."}]},{"heading":"Hydration & Electrolytes","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop strong practical knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fluid requirements"},{"text":"Sweat rate"},{"text":"Sodium losses"},{"text":"Electrolytes"},{"text":"Dehydration"},{"text":"Overhydration"},{"text":"Exercise in hot environments"},{"text":"Recovery hydration"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Practical project"},{"type":"p","text":"Measure an athlete's:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Pre-training body mass","exercise","post-training body mass"]},{"type":"p","text":"Then estimate fluid loss and develop a hydration strategy under appropriate professional supervision."}]},{"heading":"Competition Nutrition","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand the three major phases:"},{"type":"h","text":"Before competition"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Adequate energy"},{"text":"Carbohydrate availability"},{"text":"Hydration"},{"text":"Food tolerance"},{"text":"Timing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"During competition"},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on sport and duration:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fluids"},{"text":"Carbohydrates"},{"text":"Electrolytes"}]},{"type":"h","text":"After competition"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Rehydration"},{"text":"Carbohydrate restoration"},{"text":"Protein"},{"text":"Overall recovery nutrition"}]}]},{"heading":"Body Composition","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn how to understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Body weight"},{"text":"BMI limitations"},{"text":"Body-fat percentage"},{"text":"Lean mass"},{"text":"Circumferences"},{"text":"Skinfold measurements"},{"text":"Bioelectrical impedance"},{"text":"Performance-related body composition"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Do not reduce athlete performance to body weight alone."},{"type":"p","text":"For many athletes, strength, power, endurance, recovery and performance metrics are more meaningful than simply pursuing a lower body weight."}]},{"heading":"Specialisation Options","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Specialisation","Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Team Sports Nutrition"},{"text":"Cricket, football, hockey, etc."}],[{"text":"Endurance Nutrition"},{"text":"Running, cycling, swimming"}],[{"text":"Strength & Conditioning Nutrition"},{"text":"Strength, hypertrophy, power"}],[{"text":"Combat Sports Nutrition"},{"text":"Weight-class athletes"}],[{"text":"Youth Sports Nutrition"},{"text":"Adolescent athletes"}],[{"text":"Female Athlete Nutrition"},{"text":"Nutrition across training and life stages"}],[{"text":"Clinical Sports Nutrition"},{"text":"Athletes with health conditions"}],[{"text":"Performance Nutrition"},{"text":"Elite athlete performance"}],[{"text":"Sports Supplementation"},{"text":"Evidence-based supplement practice"}],[{"text":"Research"},{"text":"Sports nutrition science"}]]}]},{"heading":"Internships","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Prioritise supervised practical experience."},{"type":"h","text":"Best environments"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sports academies"},{"text":"Gyms with qualified nutrition professionals"},{"text":"High-performance centres"},{"text":"Sports medicine facilities"},{"text":"Universities"},{"text":"Professional sports teams"},{"text":"Athletic clubs"},{"text":"Hospitals with sports/clinical nutrition services"},{"text":"Fitness and wellness organisations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Athlete exposure"},{"type":"p","text":"Try to work with different athlete types:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Endurance"},{"text":"Strength"},{"text":"Team sports"},{"text":"Recreational athletes"},{"text":"Youth athletes"}]}]},{"heading":"Strong Internship Project","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"note","label":"Project","text":"Athlete Nutrition & Performance Monitoring"},{"type":"p","text":"Select an athlete or supervised training group."},{"type":"p","text":"Track:"},{"type":"table","header":["Parameter","Measurement"],"rows":[[{"text":"Body mass"},{"text":"Weekly trend"}],[{"text":"Training load"},{"text":"Sessions/week"}],[{"text":"Energy intake"},{"text":"Food records"}],[{"text":"Protein intake"},{"text":"g/day"}],[{"text":"Carbohydrate intake"},{"text":"g/day"}],[{"text":"Hydration"},{"text":"Fluid/sweat observations"}],[{"text":"Sleep"},{"text":"Hours/night"}],[{"text":"Recovery"},{"text":"Athlete-reported"}],[{"text":"Performance"},{"text":"Sport-specific metric"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"Then investigate relationships between:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Nutrition","Training","Recovery","Performance"]},{"type":"h","text":"Deliverables"},{"type":"p","text":"Create:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Athlete profile"},{"text":"Dietary assessment"},{"text":"Nutritional gaps"},{"text":"Hydration assessment"},{"text":"Performance observations"},{"text":"Evidence-based recommendations"},{"text":"Follow-up results"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Protect athlete privacy and obtain appropriate consent."}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Prioritise recognised education in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sports nutrition"},{"text":"Exercise physiology"},{"text":"Strength and conditioning"},{"text":"Nutrition counselling"},{"text":"Food safety"},{"text":"Hydration"},{"text":"Sports supplementation"},{"text":"Research methods"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Additional skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Statistical analysis"},{"text":"Nutrition analysis software"},{"text":"Research databases"},{"text":"Scientific literature evaluation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Be cautious with private “sports nutrition certifications.” Recognition, curriculum quality and scope of practice matter more than the certificate title."}]},{"heading":"Sports Supplements","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Sports Nutritionist should understand the evidence behind:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Protein supplements"},{"text":"Creatine"},{"text":"Caffeine"},{"text":"Carbohydrate products"},{"text":"Electrolytes"},{"text":"Sports drinks"},{"text":"Beta-alanine"},{"text":"Nitrate/beetroot products"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The key skill is not knowing a long list of supplements."},{"type":"p","text":"It is knowing:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Who needs it","Why","Evidence","Dose","Timing","Risk","Product quality"]}]},{"heading":"Anti-Doping Awareness","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This is essential for competitive athletes."},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Prohibited substances"},{"text":"Prohibited methods"},{"text":"Therapeutic use exemptions"},{"text":"Supplement contamination"},{"text":"Anti-doping testing"},{"text":"Athlete responsibility"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Competitive athletes can face serious consequences from contaminated supplements, so supplement selection should involve risk assessment and reliable product-quality information."}]},{"heading":"Careers You Can Be Hired As","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Possible roles include:"},{"type":"table","header":["Role","Main work"],"rows":[[{"text":"Sports Nutritionist"},{"text":"Athlete nutrition planning"}],[{"text":"Sports Nutrition Assistant"},{"text":"Support nutrition programs"}],[{"text":"Performance Nutrition Assistant"},{"text":"Training + nutrition monitoring"}],[{"text":"Athlete Nutrition Coordinator"},{"text":"Team nutrition operations"}],[{"text":"Nutrition Consultant"},{"text":"Individual nutrition support within scope"}],[{"text":"Wellness Nutritionist"},{"text":"Fitness and lifestyle nutrition"}],[{"text":"Sports Nutrition Research Assistant"},{"text":"Research studies"}],[{"text":"Nutrition Program Coordinator"},{"text":"Sports/fitness programs"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"Some clinical or regulated nutrition roles may require additional professional qualifications or registration depending on jurisdiction."}]},{"heading":"Employer / Interview Questions","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Nutrition"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"What is the role of carbohydrates in athletic performance?"},{"text":"How does muscle glycogen affect exercise?"},{"text":"Why is protein important after training?"},{"text":"What is energy availability?"},{"text":"What factors determine an athlete's energy requirements?"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Sports"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"How would nutrition differ for a marathon runner and a powerlifter?"},{"text":"How would you plan nutrition for a cricket player?"},{"text":"How would you approach a football player's match-day nutrition?"},{"text":"What causes dehydration during exercise?"},{"text":"How would you estimate sweat loss?"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Practical"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"How would you assess an athlete's diet?"},{"text":"How would you deal with an athlete who refuses to change their diet?"},{"text":"How would you evaluate a supplement claim?"},{"text":"How would you handle an athlete with a suspected nutritional deficiency?"},{"text":"When would you refer an athlete to a doctor or clinical specialist?"}]}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For advanced sports nutrition careers, postgraduate study can strengthen your scientific and professional profile."},{"type":"h","text":"Relevant PG areas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Sc. Nutrition & Dietetics"},{"text":"M.Sc. Sports Nutrition"},{"text":"M.Sc. Clinical Nutrition"},{"text":"M.Sc. Food & Nutrition"},{"text":"M.Sc. Exercise Physiology"},{"text":"M.Sc. Sports Science"},{"text":"M.Sc. Applied Nutrition"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on the institution, also consider programs in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sports science"},{"text":"Exercise science"},{"text":"Human physiology"},{"text":"Public health nutrition"}]}]},{"heading":"Clinical / Advanced Route","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"If you want to work with athletes who have medical or clinical nutrition requirements, build additional expertise in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Diabetes"},{"text":"Cardiovascular conditions"},{"text":"Gastrointestinal disorders"},{"text":"Food allergies/intolerances"},{"text":"Eating disorders"},{"text":"Renal conditions"},{"text":"Bone health"}]},{"type":"p","text":"However, medical nutrition therapy and diagnosis should remain within the legally permitted scope of practice and involve appropriate clinical professionals."}]},{"heading":"Government / Institutional Route","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Possible environments include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sports authorities"},{"text":"Government sports academies"},{"text":"Universities"},{"text":"Sports medicine centres"},{"text":"Public hospitals"},{"text":"Research institutions"},{"text":"State sports organisations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Relevant recruitment requirements can vary considerably, so verify the specific qualification and registration requirements for each post."}]},{"heading":"Study Abroad","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Relevant postgraduate programs include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MSc Sports Nutrition"},{"text":"MSc Sport and Exercise Nutrition"},{"text":"MSc Sports Science"},{"text":"MSc Exercise Physiology"},{"text":"MSc Human Nutrition"},{"text":"MSc Performance Nutrition"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Strong international research areas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Athlete recovery"},{"text":"Exercise metabolism"},{"text":"Female athlete nutrition"},{"text":"Youth athlete nutrition"},{"text":"Sports supplementation"},{"text":"Gut microbiome"},{"text":"Precision nutrition"},{"text":"Performance analytics"}]}]},{"heading":"Data-Driven Sports Nutrition","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Modern sports nutrition is increasingly quantitative."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to analyse:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Training load"},{"text":"Dietary intake"},{"text":"Body composition"},{"text":"Hydration"},{"text":"Sleep"},{"text":"Recovery"},{"text":"Performance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Example dashboard"},{"type":"flow","items":["Athlete Data","Nutrition Intake","Training Load","Hydration + Sleep","Recovery Metrics","Performance Trends","Nutrition Intervention"]},{"type":"p","text":"Tools:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"Statistical software"},{"text":"Athlete-management systems"}]}]},{"heading":"AI + Sports Nutrition","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"AI will increasingly support personalised nutrition."},{"type":"p","text":"Potential applications:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Automated food logging"},{"text":"Dietary pattern analysis"},{"text":"Athlete meal recommendations"},{"text":"Performance prediction"},{"text":"Recovery monitoring"},{"text":"Hydration prediction"},{"text":"Personalised nutrition plans"},{"text":"Wearable-data integration"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Example project"},{"type":"h","text":"AI Athlete Nutrition Dashboard"},{"type":"p","text":"Inputs:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Training load"},{"text":"Body mass"},{"text":"Dietary intake"},{"text":"Sleep"},{"text":"Hydration"},{"text":"Performance"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Output:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Nutrition trends"},{"text":"Recovery indicators"},{"text":"Potential dietary gaps"},{"text":"Athlete-specific alerts for professional review"}]},{"type":"p","text":"AI should remain a decision-support tool, not a replacement for qualified professional judgement."}]},{"heading":"Research / PhD Route","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For research-oriented students:"},{"type":"h","text":"PhD areas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Exercise metabolism"},{"text":"Sports nutrition"},{"text":"Muscle physiology"},{"text":"Nutrient timing"},{"text":"Recovery"},{"text":"Sports supplementation"},{"text":"Female athlete nutrition"},{"text":"Endurance nutrition"},{"text":"Precision nutrition"},{"text":"Gut microbiome and exercise"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential destinations:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Universities"},{"text":"Sports research institutes"},{"text":"High-performance centres"},{"text":"Nutrition companies"},{"text":"Sports science laboratories"},{"text":"Research organisations"}]}]},{"heading":"Entrepreneurship Route","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"After developing appropriate expertise and experience, possible businesses include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sports nutrition consultancy"},{"text":"Athlete meal-planning services"},{"text":"Sports nutrition education"},{"text":"Team nutrition programs"},{"text":"Nutrition analytics platforms"},{"text":"Athlete meal services"},{"text":"Sports supplement education"},{"text":"Performance nutrition technology"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong business model should be based on evidence-based practice rather than supplement sales alone."}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Performance route"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc. Nutrition & Dietetics","Sports Nutrition Intern","Nutrition Assistant","Sports Nutritionist","Senior Sports Nutritionist","Performance Nutrition Specialist","Performance Nutrition Lead"]},{"type":"h","text":"High-performance route"},{"type":"flow","items":["Sports Nutritionist","Elite Athlete Support","Team Nutrition Specialist","High-Performance Nutrition Lead","Performance Department Leadership"]},{"type":"h","text":"Research route"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc.","M.Sc.","Research Assistant","PhD","Research Scientist / Faculty","Sports Nutrition Research Lead"]}]},{"heading":"2040–2046 Evolution","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The profession is likely to move toward precision performance nutrition."},{"type":"p","text":"Traditional model:"},{"type":"h","text":"Diet plan → athlete follows plan"},{"type":"p","text":"Future model:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Athlete data","nutrition modelling","personalised intervention","continuous monitoring","performance optimisation"]},{"type":"p","text":"Emerging technologies:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Wearables"},{"text":"Continuous glucose monitoring"},{"text":"AI nutrition analysis"},{"text":"Athlete-management platforms"},{"text":"Metabolomics"},{"text":"Microbiome analysis"},{"text":"Personalised nutrition"},{"text":"Real-time hydration monitoring"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The most valuable professionals will combine:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Nutrition","Exercise Physiology","Data","Behaviour Change","Sports Science."],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Nutrition"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human nutrition"},{"text":"Biochemistry"},{"text":"Macronutrients"},{"text":"Micronutrients"},{"text":"Energy metabolism"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Sports Science"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Exercise physiology"},{"text":"Training adaptation"},{"text":"Recovery"},{"text":"Energy systems"},{"text":"Performance monitoring"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Sports Nutrition"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Competition nutrition"},{"text":"Hydration"},{"text":"Recovery"},{"text":"Body composition"},{"text":"Supplementation"},{"text":"Anti-doping"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Athlete counselling"},{"text":"Behaviour change"},{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Team collaboration"},{"text":"Ethical practice"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Python basics"},{"text":"Nutrition analysis software"},{"text":"Wearable/athlete data"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Scientific literature"},{"text":"Research methodology"},{"text":"Evidence appraisal"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Scientific writing"}]}]},{"heading":"Target Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Target"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Nutrition + physiology foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Human nutrition + assessment"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Sports nutrition + exercise physiology"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Sports internship + athlete case study"}],[{"text":"0–2 years after UG"},{"text":"Nutrition Assistant / Sports Nutrition pathway"}],[{"text":"2–5 years"},{"text":"Sports Nutritionist"}],[{"text":"5–10 years"},{"text":"Senior / Performance Nutrition Specialist"}],[{"text":"10+ years"},{"text":"Performance Nutrition Lead / Consultant / Researcher"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Best Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"A strong graduate targeting Sports Nutritionist should have:"},{"type":"p","text":"B.Sc. Nutrition & Dietetics + strong nutrition science + exercise physiology + sports-specific nutrition + hydration expertise + athlete assessment skills + supervised sports internship + evidence-based supplement knowledge + anti-doping awareness + counselling skills + research literacy + Excel/data analysis."},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest 2026-era profile is not simply someone who can create diet charts. It is a professional who can connect nutrition → training → recovery → performance, evaluate evidence critically, work safely within professional scope, and use athlete data to personalise performance-support strategies."}]}]}